{
  "id": "VA-HB-2-2024",
  "scope": "state:va",
  "title": "HB 2 Purchase, possession, sale, transfer, etc., of assault firearms and certain ammunition feeding devices prohibited; penalty",
  "urls": [
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+sum+HB0002",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+ful+HB2ER+pdf",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+vot+SV0736HB0002+HB0002",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+vot+HV1385+HB0002",
    "https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+ful+HB2ER+pdf",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+sum+HB2"
  ],
  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "New Va. Code 18.2-287.4:1(A)-(B): A. As used in this section, an \"assault firearm\" means the same as that term is defined in § 18.2-308.2:2. B. Any person who imports, sells, manufactures, purchases, or transfers an assault firearm is guilty of a Class 1 misdemeanor.\n18.2-308.2:2(F), 'Assault firearm' item 1 (page image checked; struck words removed): \"Assault firearm\" means: 1. A semi-automatic center-fire rifle or pistol that expels single or multiple projectiles by action of an explosion of a combustible material with a fixed magazine capacity in excess of 10 rounds;\n18.2-308.2:2(F), item 2: 2. A semi-automatic center-fire rifle that expels single or multiple projectiles by action of an explosion of a combustible material that has the ability to accept a detachable magazine and has one of the following characteristics: (i) a folding, telescoping, or collapsible stock; (ii) a pistol grip that protrudes conspicuously beneath the action of the rifle;\n18.2-308.2:2(F), exclusion paragraph: An \"assault firearm\" does not include any firearm that is an antique firearm, has been rendered permanently inoperable, is manually operated by bolt, pump, lever, or slide action, or was manufactured before July 1, 2024.\nNew 18.2-287.4:2(A)-(B): A. As used in this section, an \"assault firearm\" means the same as that term is defined in § 18.2-308.2:2 except that it includes such firearms manufactured before July 1, 2024. B. Any person younger than 21 years of age who imports, sells, manufactures, purchases, possesses, transports, or transfers an assault firearm is guilty of a Class 1 misdemeanor.\nNew 18.2-309.1(A)-(B): A. As used in this section, a \"large capacity ammunition feeding device\" means a magazine, belt, drum, feed strip, or similar device manufactured on or after July 1, 2024, that has a capacity of, or that can be readily restored or converted to accept, more than 10 rounds of ammunition but does not include an attached tubular device designed to accept and capable of operating only with .22 caliber rimfire ammunition. B. Any person who imports, sells, barters, or transfers a large capacity ammunition feeding device is guilty of a Class 1 misdemeanor.\n18.2-308.2:5(E) (added): E. No person shall sell an assault firearm as defined in § 18.2-308.2:2 for money, goods, services, or anything else of value.\nNew 18.2-308.1:9(B): B. Any person convicted of a violation of § 18.2-287.4:1 or 18.2-287.4:2 or this section shall be prohibited from purchasing, possessing, or transporting a firearm for three years following the date of such conviction at which point the person convicted of such offense shall no longer be prohibited from purchasing, possessing, or transporting a firearm pursuant to this section.",
  "sponsors": [
